<title>AUSTRALIA: INSTANT VIEW-Australian 1997/98 budget.</title>
<headline>INSTANT VIEW-Australian 1997/98 budget.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Treasurer Peter Costello handed down the 1997/98 Federal budget, announcing an underlying budget deficit for the fiscal year of A$3.9 billion compared and a headline budget surplus of A$6.4 billion.</p>
<p>Forecasts had centred on a underlying budget deficit of some A$2.0 billion.</p>
<p>Following are a selection of economists' immediate reactions to the budget:</p>
<p>HSBC chief economist John Edwards  </p>
<p>&quot;It is a very good budget it is a budget as expected, close to our predictions and one that we think is a pretty sensible outcome and we are not disappointed.&quot;</p>
</text>
